names></name><name><surname>Chuah</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiu</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiu</surname><given-names>YC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impact of low-residue diet on bowel preparation for colonoscopy</article-title><source>Dis Colon Rectum</source><year>2011</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>112</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21160321</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Adams</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Meagher</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lubowski</surname><given-names>DZ</given-names></name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bisacodyl reduces the volume of polyethylene glycol solution required for bowel preparation</article-title><source>Dis Colon Rectum</source><year>1994</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>233</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8137669</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Soweid</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobeissy</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jamali</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A randomized single-blind trial of standard diet versus fiber-free diet with polyethylene glycol electrolyte solution for colonoscopy preparation</article-title><source>Endoscopy</source><year>2010</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>633</fpage><lpage>638</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">20623443</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="jour